/* Modern theme for the character-creation dialog -- flat programmatic chrome, no legacy sprite
   art. Stat/description panels share the identical treatment as legacy (already flat fills in
   the original). */

/* 2026-09-03: width/height and every child's left/top below are now static RCSS instead of
   C++-pushed -- CharMakeWin.cpp's SetPosition() still pushes #panel's own left/top (a genuine
   screen-placement value, same carve-out as every other migrated window), but stopped pushing
   these, since they're constants that never actually varied at runtime (CCharMakeWin.h's own
   comment already called out the job buttons -- the one genuinely per-instance-positioned
   piece -- as "not recomputed per frame... mirrors the legacy per-class layout math exactly").
   Deliberately `px`, not `dp`, and NOT part of the global auto-fit other migrated dialogs joined
   this same pass: m_winBack (CharMakeWin.cpp) is a fixed-size CWin whose real screen position
   also drives the live 3D character-preview viewport (BeginOpengl() call in
   RenderCreateCharacter(), a completely separate, untested-here scale mechanism already reading
   m_winBack's real unscaled pixel bounds) -- growing #panel via dp without also correctly scaling
   that viewport would visibly desync the 2D chrome from the 3D preview it's meant to frame. Left
   as a documented non-scaling exception, same class as main_frame's still-legacy HUD band and
   char_info_balloon's live-projected position (layout-and-scaling.md's Fixed-vs-fluid table). */
#panel {
	position: absolute;
	width: 454px;
	height: 406px;
	font-family: "Liberation Sans";
	font-size: 12px;
	color: #d9d3c5; /* text-body */
}

#stat_panel  { left: 346px; top: 24px;  }
#desc_panel  { left: 0px;   top: 355px; }
#input_frame { left: 0px;   top: 317px; }
#btn_ok      { left: 346px; top: 325px; }
#btn_cancel  { left: 400px; top: 325px; }

.job-btn {
	position: absolute;
	width: 108px;
	height: 26px;
	text-align: center;
	vertical-align: middle;
	line-height: 26px;
	cursor: pointer;
	pointer-events: auto;
	background-color: rgba(255, 244, 224, 12); /* surface-3 */
	border: 1px rgba(140, 146, 152, 130); /* border-metal */
	border-radius: 4px; /* radius-md */
	color: #d9d3c5; /* text-body */
}
.job-btn:hover {
	background-color: rgba(140, 146, 152, 60); /* accent-gold wash */
	border: 1px #c0a050; /* accent-gold */
}
.job-btn.checked {
	background-color: #c0a050; /* accent-gold */
	border: 1px #c0a050; /* accent-gold */
	color: #efe6d3; /* text-title */
}
.job-btn.disabled {
	pointer-events: none;
	color: #9a958c; /* semantic-neutral */
	cursor: default;
	background-color: rgba(255, 244, 224, 12); /* surface-3 */
	border: 1px rgba(140, 146, 152, 130); /* border-metal */
}

.stat-panel, .desc-panel {
	position: absolute;
}
.stat-bg {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	width: 108px;
	height: 80px;
	background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 143);
}
.stat-bg.tall {
	height: 96px;
}
.desc-bg {
	position: absolute;
	left: 0;
	top: 0;
	width: 454px;
	height: 51px;
	background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 143);
}

.stat-row {
	position: absolute;
	left: 22px;
}
.stat-label {
	color: #d9d3c5; /* text-body */
}
.stat-value {
	position: absolute;
	left: 54px;
	color: #c0a050; /* accent-gold */
}

.desc-line {
	position: absolute;
	left: 10px;
	white-space: nowrap;
}

.input-frame {
	position: absolute;
	width: 346px;
	height: 38px;
	background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 110);
	border: 1px rgba(140, 146, 152, 130); /* border-metal */
	border-radius: 3px; /* radius-sm */
	pointer-events: none;
}

/* 2026-09-03: background-color/border/border-radius removed -- only width genuinely needs to
   differ from base.rcss's own .btn (54px here vs. base's 108px default) here. The removed
   `border` shorthand was silently stomping .btn-ok's crimson border-color/border-top-color back
   to gray border-metal on #btn_ok (same specificity, this file linked after base.rcss, tie always
   went to this rule) -- the fill still showed crimson (decorator, untouched) but with a
   mismatched gray border instead of a clean crimson one, same bug independently present in
   msg_win.rcss (see that file's own comment on the identical fix).

   2026-09-03, second fix: height/line-height/text-align/vertical-align now explicit here too, not
   left to inherit from base.rcss's own .btn -- that shared rule is dp now (this session's global
   auto-fit retrofit), but #panel here deliberately stays fixed px (see this file's own #panel
   comment, the 3D-viewport-coupling exception). Inheriting a dp line-height/height into a
   px-positioned, px-widthed button meant the box grew taller than its fixed width/position
   intended at any ratio other than 1.0 -- a real, screenshot-reported bug ("OK/Cancel text
   position not properly scaled"). Every property this button needs must be self-contained px now,
   matching the rest of this file's deliberate non-scaling design. */
.btn {
	position: absolute;
	width: 54px;
	height: 30px;
	text-align: center;
	vertical-align: middle;
	line-height: 30px;
	cursor: pointer;
	pointer-events: auto;
}
